  "change": "B41 plus the EA half of the beta.25 profile-staged deploy (goatai#1885, approved by Claude-Mac in 6033450916). MT5 loads every child chart from the controller-staged deploy profile at start-up; the dashboard only adopts the children it finds. A new link_children portfolio action runs one adoption pass: the TSV cid is tried first, otherwise every chart is fingerprinted once, and a child is adopted only on a one-to-one match of symbol, period, this EA, a CID record naming a free magic and a saved-template snapshot that reproduces the row's frozen SET (the settingsMatch rule, refactored to take a chart id). Adoption runs only on an inert demo terminal, persists the identity before it counts, and never opens, closes or applies anything to a chart. Rows without a child report chartId 0 and magic 0; past the 240 s start-up window the dashboard names them Not started (child_not_started in diagnostics). The template attach path is deleted (DoActivate, BuildTemplate, SaveTemplateAndCopy, DeleteCopiedTemplate, ApplyTemplate with ChartOpen/ChartApplyTemplate, NewSingleInstance, AgentDeployRow, DeployAll and the kernel32 copy/delete imports); deploy_next gets the refusal rejected_deploy_next_retired; Activate and Deploy All show \"Use Next in the app to deploy; dashboard deploy returns in the next update\". CA41 (ported from 4f3f2f9 only): six WriteSet-omitted inputs accepted by the audit at their declared defaults. No trade logic, input, default, WriteSet, trade-event policy, bias wire or model route changes: the entrypoint differs from B41 only in its build ID and marker, and every other closure file except the dashboard, the setup control and the child audit is byte-identical to B41.",
